      "sequence_position": 3,
      "problem": "In rectangle $ABCD$, $AB=18$ and $BC=9.$ Find $|\\overset{\\to }{BD}|.$",
      "worked_solution": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251078/assets/3e03c8d3377aef27d7542ef2d734ebd64d00bbc1539e63222b7df9abc696bd44.png)\n\nAs we can see from the picture above, in $△BAD$ we have $∠BAD={90}^{∘}$, $AB=18$ and $AD=BC=9.$ So, the Pythagorean theorem gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\overset{\\to }{BD}| & =BD \\\\  & =\\sqrt{A{B}^{2}+A{D}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{18}^{2}+{9}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{405} \\\\  & =9\\sqrt{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $|\\overset{\\to }{BD}|=9\\sqrt{5}.$",
